ho discovered him as a kid<br /> \u200breasom for the vigil is they want to rule and these monsters are in the way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T07:16:47-07:00","id":1110536,"title":"","content":"So nobody other then vento has talked about the endowment and really i need imfo about this so criticism is welcome just try to explain to help me know what to do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T08:05:54-07:00","id":1110547,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13426\" data-vbnamecard=\"13426\">Ameraaaaaa</a>: I think people just aren't enthusiastic about the current write-up. Try flavoring it up, adding some interesting bits, complexity, and conflict.<br /> For me, at least, the concept of a group of immortals plotting world domination is boring (it has been done before, so often it is trite), and why they would really be involved in the Vigil is questionable. Combine that with their one-trick Endowment, and they seem more like an Antagonist group than a PC Conspiracy. They might make a decent source Conspiracy for Deviant, though.<br /> <br /> Or people are turned away at your posts' general lack of formatting and grammar. I know it isn't easy given your input medium, but someone not being able to quickly read and make sense of a post increases the chance they will just not bother. I get that way with walls of text. Not having even basic punctuation, spelling, and grammar signals to many that the poster just doesn't bother (so why should they). PS4 wasn't really designed around typing, so it doesn't have the degree of tools and correction that most users are used to - you might have to take extra effort to do all the correction yourself before posting (or go back and edit afterwards, if you are focused on just getting your thoughts down immediately).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T08:56:34-07:00","id":1110562,"title":"","content":"I sea understood ok so what about making them a fromer group of alchemists from greminy and maybe more details also is the endowment really that boring i know it only dos one thing but it dos it well so i thought it would be liked but i guess thats how it works well any flavor you can think of maybe there were with the allied forces because there leader ws not ahyen like the nazi thought were superior so thats flavor any more ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T13:49:23-07:00","id":1110650,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Alchemists seeking immortality is a pretty standard Promethean antagonist. Germans with ties to what happened in World War II is already parallel with the Loyalists of Thule. I'd look elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Have you seen Netflix's Daredevil (season 2) and Iron Fist (season 1)? Maybe you could tie them into a group like the Hand, except one that has already found their Black Sky long ago (the immortal). Of course, that still makes them more Antagonistic than the Vigil players usually are. Maybe make them closer to the Lucifuge in concept, and make them rebel against a darker purpose (either the PC Conspiracy is rebelling against the core group, or the group itself - immortal included - is defying their purpose). As for a source, maybe a Cthonic God, deep in the Underworld? The group's immortality is part of a pact - death itself rejects them so that they can further their &quot;master's&quot; objective(s). If you wanted to expand upon their abilities (beyond resurrection), you could grant them various deathly, psychopomply, or related abilities. As a risk/counter-balance, actually using them might risk their immortality, as the Underworld God's minions might locate them easier (making the risk closer to a Demon's Compromise).<br /> EDIT: Which, admittedly, sounds very close to a Sin-Eater, but does differ on the fine details.<br /> <br /> Just some ideas. Try researching other historical or mythological attempts at immortality (like Koschei's method) for inspiration. Make your group tangentially related, give them a reason to fight monsters, and see where that takes you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-02-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T21:49:43-07:00","id":1110756,"title":"","content":"The 2ed idea and 3ed ideas of rebels a gods sound good and endowment idea sounds good as well but now im wered about it being op so might keep the stamina cost to even it out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T00:47:15-07:00","id":1110781,"title":"","content":"Maybe something like this every dot adds to the revevfy dread power as well as a extra benefits for every dot <br /> 1sr dot lets you hear twilight <br /> 2ed lets you see twilight <br /> 3ed dot let let's entity in twilight hear you but not see you <br /> 4th dot lets you touch entity in twilight <br /> 5th dot lets you eat ghosts to gain temporary power might change this but how you like it so far","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T02:16:41-07:00","id":1110790,"title":"","content":"Never mind its just like the 4 dot endowment from chen group but with revefy so do you have any idea might remove the dread power but for now we have alchemists who found an immortal baby then implanted some of hes blood into theres and went agenst the nazi even though there were gremen and then the kid grow up to lead the conspiracy and plans 2 rule the world <br /> foot notes 1 they droped the baby on purpose to test if he was immortal 2 the babys blood refill right away 3 the leader has black haired and black eyed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T04:23:31-07:00","id":1110797,"title":"","content":"Random thoughts<br /> 1. Eating ghosts for powers gives them a reason to hunt ghosts - likely need other reason for hunting other monsters.<br /> 2. Powers should probably be condensed down into 1 - it's too asymmetric at a spread of 5 dots, with the first few being barely noticeable increases, and the 5th a dramatic jump.<br /> 3. If stay with German Alchemists, I'd have them be older than WWII.<br /> 4. Black eyed, you say? Dark Irises, or full on solid black eyes? Like maybe the Black-Eyed Kids in the Horrors section of the CofD Core book?<br /> 5. I had an idea about a group that used injected serums to take on the traits of monsters (Dread Power set, in Hunter terms). Downsides was becoming more monstrous over time, but that makes them less viable long term characters. If you want, you could use the idea for this group - they develop Serum from monsters, which lets a human take on their powers... at the cost of becoming more like said monster with repeated use. This group corrects that by killing their own members first - but thanks to the pre-existing Revivify power, this is merely a reset instead of outright ending. The Serum isn't desirable to other groups (like Cheiron) due to the side effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-03-2017, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T04:45:08-07:00","id":1110799,"title":"","content":"1 i will save for another conspiracy<br /> 2 true<br /> 3 there are as old as barbarians older its mysterious<br /> 4 irises but full black sounds interesting<br /> 5 ok so wait revefy is random chance so why risk it <br /> so no back to old idea and giving him full black eyes and Chinese i want Japanese but i think Chinese makes a good competition sence the Mongols are barbarians but kidnapped Japanese prince might work maybe make make them Japanese conspiracy whatever but still allied forces","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T05:53:39-07:00","id":1110808,"title":"","content":"The Dice Pool isn't that hard, and they can re-attempt it if